<decompilertest>
<!--
    cleanupcode: delete the Rust drop/deallocate call sites (a port of the idea in
    SEFCOM Oxidizer's CleanupCodeRemover, whose STAGE is BEFORE_VARIABLE_RECOVERY).
    Rust emits a drop-glue call at every scope exit and every `?` early return, so
    decompiled Rust is dominated by `core::ptr::drop_in_place(...)` lines that appear
    nowhere in the source.  Stage model: S2, a classification of a direct CALL by the
    callee's identity (the family `funcboundflow` / `noreturn_extern` sit in).

    Layout (linked flat, x86-64 SysV):
      caller        @ 0x100040 : v = real_work(); DROP(0x11223344); DEALLOC(0x55667788);
                                 return a0 + v;
      real_work     @ 0x100070 : return 0x42;                      // a REAL call, kept
      drop_in_place @ 0x100080 : ret                               // generic-suffixed name
      __rust_dealloc@ 0x100090 : ret                               // plain name

    The two `mov edi, <const>` argument setups feed nothing but the cleanup calls, so
    they are the load-bearing part of the test: the pass runs in the PRE-SSA window, so
    once the CALL is destroyed those writes lose their last reader and the ordinary
    ActionDeadCode fixpoint collects them.  A removal done after SSA would leave both
    constants behind as unexplained assignments.

    Pass 1 (default, cleanupcode on): the whole function collapses to
    `return a0 + real_work();`.
    Pass 2 (option cleanupcode off, the pre-feature rendering): both cleanup calls and
    both argument constants are back, and the call result spills to a named temporary.

    Asserts #1 to #4 each pin a line to EXACTLY ONE occurrence across the two print C
    passes: present in the cleanupcode-off pass, absent in the default pass.  Assert #5
    pins `real_work` to BOTH passes, so the transform is surgical: it deletes the two
    listed callees and nothing else.  Note the callee is matched on its NORMALIZED path
    (generic arguments stripped), which is why the escaped
    `$LT$alloc..string..String$GT$` suffix does not defeat the match.
-->
